---
description: Authoring the design system's CSS
globs: ['packages/core/src/**/*.css']
alwaysApply: false
---

- One component per file in `src/components/`, added to `_index.css`.
- Layers nest and deeper is weaker: `@layer badge.l1.l2.l3` (foundation),
  `.l1.l2` (variant), `.l1` (state). Never flatten to siblings — sibling layers
  order by first appearance, so moving a block changes what wins.
- The first layer segment is the bundle name; the build reads it to attribute
  the rule.
- `src/base/` emits tokens and no classes. A utility placed there becomes
  invisible compile context and never ships.
- A derived token gets its fallback at the point of use
  (`var(--radius-button, var(--radius-field))`), never a `:root` default — a
  custom property's `var()` resolves where it is declared, so a `:root` default
  freezes the root's value and a theme override never reaches it.

After any change: `bun run --filter '@scope/project-name' check`.
